# Kavacha patch 0056 — customization follow-ups (REMAINING_WORK.md §3
# "Customization": light themes, CSS syntax highlighting, active-tab emphasis
# and tab-strip spacing, first-launch coach mark).
#
# 1. LIGHT THEMES. ADR 0008 recorded the real obstacle: patch 0016 bridges
#    Kavacha into Zen with `--zen-branding-dark: var(--kavacha-surface)` plus a
#    column of `light-dark(stock-light, var(--kavacha-*))`, so overriding the
#    base tokens only ever fills the DARK half — a bright surface produced
#    dark-derived chrome with light text on it. The fix is NOT to duplicate
#    that mapping in JS. The engine derives a mode from the theme's own surface
#    luminance and stamps kavacha-theme-mode on the chrome root;
#    kavacha-theme-light.inc.css owns the light half, mirroring what 0016 does
#    for the dark half. CSS keeps the mapping, the engine keeps the decision,
#    and because the mode is DERIVED rather than declared, user and marketplace
#    theme packages get light support without declaring anything — and a
#    package that claimed "light" while shipping a near-black surface cannot
#    produce unreadable chrome. The threshold is the same 0.45 the engine
#    already used to pick color-scheme, kept identical so the two cannot
#    disagree. One built-in light theme ships as the proof.
#
# 2. CSS SYNTAX HIGHLIGHTING. A textarea cannot render styled text, so the
#    textarea stays the real editing surface — caret, selection, undo, IME,
#    spellcheck and screen-reader support all remain native — and is made
#    transparent over a scroll-synced <pre> that paints the colours. Nothing
#    about editing is reimplemented, so nothing about editing can regress. The
#    tokens are built with createElement/createTextNode: about:studio runs with
#    the SYSTEM PRINCIPAL, so assigning the user's CSS to innerHTML would be
#    script execution with chrome privileges. Above 60k characters the
#    highlighting drops to plain text rather than building a span per token on
#    every keystroke — the editor is the textarea, so that is a degradation,
#    not a failure.
#
# 3. ACTIVE-TAB EMPHASIS + SPACING. At the shipped horizontal density the
#    selected tab differed from its neighbours by a few percent of luminance,
#    which on a laptop panel at an angle is genuinely ambiguous. Emphasis now
#    runs on three independent channels — surface, label weight, and an accent
#    rail — so it survives any one being washed out. The rail is an inset
#    box-shadow, not a border, so it costs no layout and cannot shift the strip
#    as selection moves.
#
# 4. FIRST-LAUNCH COACH MARK. Patch 0030 added the menu button precisely
#    because every feature was Cmd+K-only — but an unexplained gear leaves a
#    user who never presses it exactly where they were. Shown ONCE per profile,
#    non-modal, noautofocus, closing on its own: it is an explanation, and
#    interrupting someone to explain a button they have not asked about is
#    worse than the button being unexplained. The pref flips BEFORE the panel
#    is shown, so a crash between the two cannot resurrect it, and never in a
#    private window, which is not anyone's first launch.
#
# ALSO FIXED, found by auditing every zen-icons/selectable reference against
# the jar manifest rather than by looking at the UI: eleven palette and menu
# entries pointed at selectable/clock.svg and selectable/window.svg, neither of
# which exists in the icon set or the jar. They have rendered as missing images
# since patches 0013/0022/0023/0025/0028/0029. Re-pointed at time.svg, layers.svg
# and shapes.svg, all of which are packaged. The audit is now clean.
#
# Why a patch: the theme bridge, the Studio page, the tab strip and the menu
# button are all Zen/Kavacha chrome sources with no pref or overlay equivalent.
#
# Touches: src/zen/common/sys/KavachaThemeEngine.sys.mjs,
#          src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-theme-light.inc.css (new) + zen-theme.css,
#          src/zen/kavacha-studio/{studio.html,studio.js,studio.css},
#          src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-polish.inc.css,
#          src/zen/common/sys/KavachaMenu.sys.mjs + kavacha-menu.inc.css,
#          src/zen/common/sys/{KavachaCommandRegistry,KavachaMarketplace,
#            KavachaPluginManager,KavachaSDK}.sys.mjs (icon fixes),
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl.
# Applies on top of 0055.
